:: Credits [academic]
<div class="academic-page">
<h1>Credits</h1>
<p class="subtitle">The Kremlin Files · prototype, November 2026</p>

<h2>Project</h2>

Concept, historical research direction and design decisions: Aiden Smith, Digital Humanities, University of Tennessee. Developed with the assistance of Claude, an AI model by Anthropic, in Claude Code. An AI use log documents that collaboration.

<h2>Software</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>SugarCube 2</strong> story format, by Thomas Michael Edwards: BSD 2-Clause License.</li>
<li><strong>Tweego</strong> compiler, by Thomas Michael Edwards: BSD 2-Clause License.</li>
<li><strong>Twine 2</strong>, by Chris Klimas and contributors: GPL-3.0. The source is compatible with the Twine 2 editor.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Fonts</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>PT Serif, PT Sans Narrow, PT Mono</strong>, by ParaType: SIL Open Font License 1.1, served by Google Fonts.</li>
<li><strong>Marck Script</strong>, by Denis Masharov: SIL Open Font License 1.1, served by Google Fonts.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Images</h2>

All visual elements (the desk, telephone, terminal, stamps and paper) are drawn with original CSS and SVG. No photographs or third-party images are used.

